  "description": "The target community is individuals who are familiar with antisemitic stereotypes, particularly those who may find humor in or be drawn to offensive, hateful content. The meme is designed to provoke and offend, likely targeting an audience that either enjoys or is desensitized to antisemitic tropes, or who may be seeking to shock or mock Jewish people through the use of derogatory stereotypes. The visual context of a holiday dinner (turkey, Christmas tree) is used to contrast with the hateful text, which may appeal to an audience that finds irony or dark humor in juxtaposing festive imagery with offensive messages. The use of crude language ('i fuckin told you!') suggests the target audience may include those who appreciate or are accustomed to vulgar, confrontational humor.",
